# Ownership graph + experiments / tests umbrella

Phase 2 of the multi-tenant rollout. Postgres is the canonical store;
Neo4j is the secondary projection. Hard rules 33-34 in
[AGENTS.md](mdc:AGENTS.md) are the source of truth.

## Reads

- Anything that traverses **more than one hop** of the ownership
  graph (User -> Team -> Workspace -> Project -> Resource, etc.)
  goes through
  [`OwnershipGraphStore.traverse`](mdc:aqp/graph/protocol.py) or the
  `data.ownership.*` MCP tools. Don't hand-write the recursive
  Postgres join — it will diverge from the Neo4j projection.
- The Postgres store ([`PostgresOwnershipGraphStore`](mdc:aqp/graph/postgres_store.py))
  is the bootstrap / fallback when `AQP_OWNERSHIP_GRAPH_STORE=postgres`
  (the default). The Neo4j store ([`Neo4jOwnershipGraphStore`](mdc:aqp/graph/neo4j_store.py))
  takes over when the env var is `neo4j`.
- `data.ownership.list_resources` defaults to **ctx.actor**; tools
  passing an explicit `user_id` MUST be admin-scoped.

## Writes

- All ownership writes flow through the canonical ORM models
  ([`Membership`](mdc:aqp/persistence/models_tenancy.py),
  [`Experiment`](mdc:aqp/persistence/models_experiments.py),
  [`Test`](mdc:aqp/persistence/models_experiments.py),
  [`Resource`](mdc:aqp/persistence/models_resources.py),
  [`ResourceRelation`](mdc:aqp/persistence/models_resources.py)).
- The SQLAlchemy
  [`after_flush_postexec`](mdc:aqp/graph/sqlalchemy_hooks.py) hooks
  translate every commit into [`OwnershipEvent`](mdc:aqp/graph/events.py)
  rows on the `aqp:ownership:events` Redis stream. The
  [`drain_events`](mdc:aqp/tasks/ownership_tasks.py) Celery task
  consumes them in batches of `ownership_sync_batch_size`.
- The periodic [`full_resync`](mdc:aqp/tasks/ownership_tasks.py)
  task rebuilds the Neo4j projection from Postgres. Idempotent;
  safe to run while the API is serving.

## Experiments + Tests umbrella

- Every new run-producing flow MUST populate `experiment_id` (and
  `test_id` where applicable) on its run row — see hard rule 34.
- Migration 0037 added the FK columns to every existing typed run
  table. New `*_runs` tables in future migrations MUST include the
  FK from day one.
- The [`LedgerWriter`](mdc:aqp/persistence/ledger.py) `_stamp` chain
  copies `RequestContext.experiment_id` / `.test_id` onto run rows
  automatically — most flows just need a populated context.

## Polymorphic Resources

- The `resources` table is the universal handle for any content
  asset that isn't already a first-class ORM (datasets / bots /
  agents get their own).
- Ownership is polymorphic via `(owner_scope_kind, owner_scope_id)` —
  see :data:`OWNER_SCOPE_KINDS` in
  [`models_resources`](mdc:aqp/persistence/models_resources.py).
- The ownership-graph projector translates the Resource into a
  `(:OwnerKind)-[:OWNS]->(:Resource)` edge in Neo4j.
- Strategy templates (Phase 7 LEAN ingester) use this table with
  `resource_type='strategy_template'`; see
  [strategy-templates.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/strategy-templates.mdc).

## Don't list

- Don't hand-write multi-hop joins over the tenancy / experiment /
  resource tables — go through `OwnershipGraphStore`.
- Don't bypass `after_flush_postexec` to write directly to Neo4j;
  the bus is the only sanctioned ingress.
- Don't write to `aqp:ownership:events` from outside
  [`aqp/graph/events.py`](mdc:aqp/graph/events.py).
- Don't add a new `*_runs` table without an `experiment_id` FK.

